      the player from falling off the front or back of the map by constantly setting
      its Z position to 0, the centre of the world.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c13976e4-772e-45cc-8886-b21e34101c69","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7576.0,"yMin":98.0,"xMax":-7480.0,"yMax":162.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"00d07eee-99d6-4e1c-8d67-09e323485f6c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3436.0,"yMin":-114.0,"xMax":-3336.0,"yMax":-24.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is grounded, don''t move downwards.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"e6ef0479-c3b9-4c19-a9a5-8272e6017139","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7618.0,"yMin":4783.0,"xMax":-7437.0,"yMax":4876.0},"title":"Player
      Display","body":"Get the Canvas that has all the UI elements on it. Hardcoded
      indices are bad practice but I am lazy.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"74adc13d-d37c-47b9-aea6-cd5dd53b8253","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7204.0,"yMin":4790.0,"xMax":-7031.0,"yMax":4884.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Set its fill to the percentage calculated earlier. This makes
      only the first x percent visible.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"4b6d24c4-7bac-418e-abbe-80d78cdcdd7f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4323.333,"yMin":2331.0,"xMax":-4131.0,"yMax":2436.333},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds nothing, the player is not grounded. It is
      still called GravityGrounded from an older version of the jump system.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"be2bcd56-207e-466f-abbe-24ae8351dcbb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3526.0,"yMin":1250.0,"xMax":-3282.333,"yMax":1360.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Run
      a cooldown for the defined amount of time. While it runs, update the cooldown
      percent variable for the indicator. Once it finishes, allow the player to dash
      again.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"2b046fea-6238-4d9e-88ce-befcaf137d75","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8761.0,"yMin":-561.0,"xMax":-8638.0,"yMax":-441.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"Activate
      all the object variables for consistency across scenes. I have noted all their
      units.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"eb80ec44-2936-4296-a9c7-fd7d8d8111c9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-1558.0,"yMin":-105.0,"xMax":-1423.0,"yMax":-30.0},"title":"Movement","body":"After
      all that, move the player with the calculated speed.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9e86260b-d9b7-4cbf-9478-cc10c84f82ef","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7710.0,"yMin":-548.0,"xMax":-7614.0,"yMax":-484.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"d85d8e36-ffa7-4be1-84db-463696cb76d5","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2185.0,"yMin":159.0,"xMax":-2031.0,"yMax":223.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Then
