      the player is pressing Jump and they haven''t used all their jumps...","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"33222291-ee51-4967-97e4-bbfecbb0635e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2591.0,"yMin":4206.0,"xMax":-2480.0,"yMax":4283.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Wait
      until the animation is finished.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"baae3409-5dab-4990-8233-d9a1293f429c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4808.0,"yMin":4451.0,"xMax":-4588.0,"yMax":4605.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"If
      we are not currently animating an attack, check if any attack inputs are pressed,
      and which one. The convenient Switch node selects a flow based on the current
      input. These systems are basically identical, so I will only comment the top
      one.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"a45df6b3-b856-4cf3-be6f-decde6a613b0","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-9690.0,"yMin":2937.0,"xMax":-9506.0,"yMax":3001.0},"title":"Sticky
