      the animator to play the respective animation.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"38ea13f0-09fb-4c27-80ad-fa80c8b0e6de","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8139.0,"yMin":4765.0,"xMax":-7981.0,"yMax":4859.0},"title":"UI
      Display","body":"Controls the UI elements of the player. Currently, health
      bar and dash cooldown.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"b64987ad-401b-4e97-b4ad-3a6de88d3b48","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8173.0,"yMin":4358.0,"xMax":-8014.0,"yMax":4454.0},"title":"Hurt","body":"Triggered
      by things that deal damage. Just changes health by the given damage.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c5411e3b-0936-4e21-a32e-923df96d7f08","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7837.0,"yMin":332.0,"xMax":-7741.0,"yMax":396.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"6ed7381e-7942-4ae5-b695-4495508fbf2e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4110.0,"yMin":1588.0,"xMax":-3972.0,"yMax":1676.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Add
      a count to the number of dashes and turn off the button input press.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"38657199-a64d-4e77-b97b-7f7a3ee42606","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3914.0,"yMin":-394.0,"xMax":-3724.0,"yMax":-305.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Make
      the player jump by adding the calculated jump force to Motion, then move the
      character with Motion.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"834ea1f1-48c3-4e15-bc28-a7227ac25f7c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3638.0,"yMin":5849.0,"xMax":-3469.0,"yMax":5940.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Otherwise,
      (if the player is on the ground) turn the animator back on if it isn''t already.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"6fe0b18c-10c2-458b-9aa0-99f1dcd97e74","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4920.0,"yMin":3426.0,"xMax":-4757.0,"yMax":3545.0},"title":"Attack
      Animations","body":"This system is very temporary. It only animates, it doesn''t
      do any attacking. If it makes it into a commit, don''t touch it.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"c88670b4-dd92-404f-a2ac-60dfe3f04837","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4664.0,"yMin":177.0,"xMax":-4419.0,"yMax":287.0},"title":"Gravity","body":"When
      the player isn''t on the ground, they should accelerate towards it. To do this,
      get the current velocity and the constant gravity, make them into m/timestep,
      and add them up.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"d31392d4-e184-4235-acaf-da82c29901dc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4091.0,"yMin":5788.0,"xMax":-3972.0,"yMax":5877.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Do
      the same thing with the down-jumping sprite.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"31c0d722-45e7-4422-8bc7-f4cadc917967","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7899.0,"yMin":5031.0,"xMax":-7782.0,"yMax":5124.0},"title":"Health
      Bar","body":"Store the current amount of health as a float from 0-1.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"c13e46a3-f180-49fa-9a13-4dd53d897dc3","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7808.0,"yMin":100.0,"xMax":-7712.0,"yMax":164.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"a8062e97-2d9b-4aac-8ae0-e927d8e21f14","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6401.0,"yMin":3414.0,"xMax":-6247.667,"yMax":3507.0},"title":"Animations","body":"This
      big flow is for animating the player (or currently the stick), every frame.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"51ade278-49d8-46ca-8397-873fd1af7490","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8561.0,"yMin":96.0,"xMax":-8465.0,"yMax":160.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"642ae9cb-aea9-467c-beec-49ee2d3dadd8","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7007.0,"yMin":5157.0,"xMax":-6869.0,"yMax":5239.0},"title":"Dash
      Cooldown","body":"This variable is controlled in the movement script.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"f573e478-acc2-43df-9265-db3590badb80","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6419.0,"yMin":-723.0,"xMax":-6232.0,"yMax":-641.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Scale the player input with respect to physics times and acceleration
      speed.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"8795115f-c03d-4684-bf27-4e1b8d1a08f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5274.0,"yMin":-250.0,"xMax":-5085.333,"yMax":-141.0},"title":"Movement","body":"The
      Motion variable is what eventually gets used to move the player. First, it
      is set to the accelerating movement input.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a94951ba-ecbe-47d5-967a-037061522762","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8515.0,"yMin":333.0,"xMax":-8419.0,"yMax":397.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"c2d710dd-2947-48e2-93f7-169b7caffd5e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6467.0,"yMin":32.0,"xMax":-6285.0,"yMax":136.0},"title":"Display
      MaxSpeed","body":"This calculates the max speed of the player based on drag
      and acceleration speed. It is \"displayed\" as an object variable.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"7114167e-fbc2-4585-a9bf-7f5a5cc91fb7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3527.0,"yMin":4183.0,"xMax":-3355.0,"yMax":4271.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Tell
      the graph (and by extension, the animator) we are animating, and turn off the
      input.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"5b4f422a-50ea-44be-8f3a-fe87919eb03d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2558.0,"yMin":-264.0,"xMax":-2345.667,"yMax":-172.5185},"title":"Movement","body":"Create
      the illusion of terminal velocity by clamping y velocity to a negative limit.
      The player can go up as fast as they want.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"9959c1a7-811f-460c-a142-6c00ba95de82","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5343.0,"yMin":3943.0,"xMax":-5128.0,"yMax":4048.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Tell
      the animator if the player is moving. The animator doesn''t actually care which
      way they are moving, it just cares whether they are or not.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"b27d58c0-7ee0-4893-889a-5edfcad28ab4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8044.0,"yMin":-317.0,"xMax":-7948.0,"yMax":-253.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"d9d2f7f3-e7ed-40f2-a99e-cf3884737e01","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8064.0,"yMin":328.0,"xMax":-7968.0,"yMax":392.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"8a45e75d-cc28-45c9-8173-8636d3db6d1a","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3788.0,"yMin":149.0,"xMax":-3615.0,"yMax":227.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player wants to fast fall, set their velocity instantly to terminal.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"bb915bd9-4289-4f01-bd6c-3cd1a918b1bf","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3514.0,"yMin":-508.0,"xMax":-3350.0,"yMax":-428.0},"title":"Movement","body":"Add
      a count to the number of jumps and turn off the jump button.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"94bf0010-fe68-4eed-9c8c-b064660906f7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8042.0,"yMin":94.0,"xMax":-7946.0,"yMax":158.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"9d3eceb4-b300-45d6-91ba-e2502a06c559","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8446.0,"yMin":3232.0,"xMax":-8295.0,"yMax":3296.0},"title":"Visuals","body":"This
      half controls the UI and animations.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"f08138f1-344e-447d-b196-a8a77e067be7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6313.0,"yMin":3917.0,"xMax":-6182.0,"yMax":3994.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Makes
      the stick run relative to movement speed.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"3dee5e80-d03d-410e-a211-578162501c4a","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8469.0,"yMin":653.0,"xMax":-8373.0,"yMax":717.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"d23a4d22-8673-4820-bc87-dd6ceece40b4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7790.0,"yMin":-319.0,"xMax":-7694.0,"yMax":-255.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"82913233-80d9-4ee9-a89b-8ea4e3bc4b9e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7582.0,"yMin":324.0,"xMax":-7445.0,"yMax":388.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres/second","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"b0585c79-f766-4924-8a8f-dc113e38de4f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8076.0,"yMin":1380.0,"xMax":-7926.0,"yMax":1472.0},"title":"Inputs","body":"Tells
      the graph when the player is trying to jump, dash, fastfall or attack.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"95b35221-73b6-46f2-aeb9-91ac3ffda104","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4679.0,"yMin":1998.0,"xMax":-4484.0,"yMax":2107.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"This lovely node checks if there is anything within the box
      just defined. The Layer Mask means anything not in that layer will be ignored.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"b0759b95-1179-414c-bd47-3ea7a7dd0c0e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7960.0,"yMin":-548.0,"xMax":-7864.0,"yMax":-484.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"38a421d8-993f-4ff8-b99b-2cd18cdf02cb","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4906.0,"yMin":6013.0,"xMax":-4539.0,"yMax":6104.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Turn
      off the animator so it isn''t trying to set the sprite, and manually set the
      sprite to the up-jumping one. If we make an animation for jumping and falling,
      this entire system will be redone, but my stolen sprites don''t have air animations.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"a5170fef-38a8-47d7-9878-ded7fe76e196","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5038.0,"yMin":2057.0,"xMax":-4883.0,"yMax":2136.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"Get a point that is a bit more than halfway down the player.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"e71c0329-35a1-44c5-80ad-d8bd94b1b079","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2868.0,"yMin":157.0,"xMax":-2519.667,"yMax":251.0},"title":"Drag","body":"Calculates
      drag.\nThe formula is velocity / ( 1 + Drag ), with a delta time because Unity
      stores everything in m/s not timestep. Y drag never worked out properly, so
      it is disconnected.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"474c5565-6804-4b2d-8e90-dbf8b51c71d4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4310.0,"yMin":1902.0,"xMax":-4084.0,"yMax":2016.667},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"If the box finds something, the player is grounded, so stops
      accelerating downwards, turns off the fastfall toggle, and regains all their
      jumps and dashes.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"1534c3c1-4511-40b9-85b8-a540a687e69b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8290.0,"yMin":96.0,"xMax":-8194.0,"yMax":160.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"48f42ed5-ff18-499e-8220-52e0c52da54c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7575.0,"yMin":-320.0,"xMax":-7479.0,"yMax":-256.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"d2bb17e5-25c6-40d1-9411-76b0eb964018","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5541.0,"yMin":-745.0,"xMax":-5351.0,"yMax":-678.0},"title":"Input
      Scale","body":"Add the current velocity in units/timestep to accelerate.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"1e93d8ec-48de-4e41-9571-e54275bd4663","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5378.0,"yMin":4382.0,"xMax":-5114.0,"yMax":4517.0},"title":"Moving","body":"If
      the player has velocity but isn''t pushing an input, they will animate idle.
      This makes them animate idle while moving for a moment, but it isn''t very
      noticeable and is better than the alternative, animating very slowly as the
      character stops from drag.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"63df4471-6bae-4c27-8cd8-d082ef7cca27","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8263.0,"yMin":-553.0,"xMax":-8126.0,"yMax":-489.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres/second","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"7ce45d6c-1f65-43ac-9ecf-b71d16e9404c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7143.0,"yMin":2451.0,"xMax":-6959.0,"yMax":2516.0},"title":"Inputs","body":"There
      is a   space   in this box. Please don''t touch it.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"56246ae2-f6ed-47ca-afdc-da0c477ef435","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8415.0,"yMin":3370.0,"xMax":-8201.0,"yMax":3491.0},"title":"Animation
      Direction","body":"A little bit of logic that flips the character around (using
      negative scale) and stores the current facing direction. Does it twice for
      now, once for the nice Camille and once for the stick.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"a13ca175-0663-4ff2-9233-6efca5b8dca2","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5717.0,"yMin":3951.0,"xMax":-5514.0,"yMax":4042.0},"title":"Moving","body":"If
      the player is moving, tell the animator that. The animator multiplies the animation
      speed by this value.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"64128d06-def1-4d34-85da-63a4b3cc3687","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5539.0,"yMin":1158.0,"xMax":-5361.333,"yMax":1295.0},"title":"Dash","body":"First,
      check the player can dash. Make sure they are pushing the button, they haven''t
      dashed the maximum number of times, and they aren''t already dashing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"59c87fab-90d2-45ae-a177-6b4632295162","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7031.0,"yMin":-820.0,"xMax":-6853.0,"yMax":-738.0},"title":"Movement","body":"This
      bit controls gravity, drag, and player walking and jumping.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"88859bb0-6601-40da-9ba7-50d08f832800","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6005.0,"yMin":4302.0,"xMax":-5816.333,"yMax":4406.0},"title":"Moving","body":"Scale
      the animation speed by velocity times something small. This will need tweaking
      when we have proper animations.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"59197339-53f9-4d25-97aa-b3d91e8ec907","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4515.0,"yMin":1108.0,"xMax":-4197.0,"yMax":1232.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Calculate
      how far the player will dash by multiplying the distance by direction (positive
      for right, negative for left, 0 goes nowhere). Then add that to the velocity
      in m/timestep. If the player isn''t giving an input or the character isn''t
      moving, dashing consumes a charge but does nothing.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"04830f34-b424-4a5f-aa67-b0cad8b7dae4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4305.0,"yMin":1296.0,"xMax":-4148.0,"yMax":1361.0},"title":"Dash","body":"Move
      the player with that calculated force.","colorTheme":"Teal","guid":"cbe3a90b-dc1e-4da6-83c7-1cf2bc14b022","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4460.0,"yMin":5806.0,"xMax":-4354.0,"yMax":5885.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"If
      the player''s y velocity is negative...","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"41c21d1e-9cfc-494a-ad47-3616ff0b615f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6901.0,"yMin":4807.0,"xMax":-6684.0,"yMax":4887.0},"title":"Dash
      Cooldown","body":"Do the same thing for the dash cooldown indicator, which
      is circular but works the same way.","colorTheme":"Blue","guid":"bd0af0bd-5395-4f43-aec7-2da502dbdb5f","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-6491.0,"yMin":2224.0,"xMax":-6309.0,"yMax":2314.0},"title":"Inputs","body":"Fastfall
      is effectively a toggle, it turns off once the player hits the ground, the
      player can''t turn it off.","colorTheme":"Purple","guid":"b20b1bbc-955c-40d5-bd90-b432d886082e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5447.0,"yMin":5878.0,"xMax":-5325.0,"yMax":5973.0},"title":"Jumping","body":"Makes
      the sprite change how it looks when it jumps.","colorTheme":"Red","guid":"c3d63f0f-7aec-4f04-8c58-33da45c7725c","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5603.0,"yMin":1894.0,"xMax":-5447.667,"yMax":1969.0},"title":"Grounded
      Check","body":"Check if the player is grounded for gravity and jump reasons.","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"0a690392-568a-420a-b5ef-e38c3752a10d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-3381.0,"yMin":351.0,"xMax":-3190.0,"yMax":432.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is not grounded, accelerate them towards the ground.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"91df67b4-f70a-4dec-b0b7-fb7151e53936","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-2371.0,"yMin":4195.0,"xMax":-2171.0,"yMax":4298.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"Tell
      the graph and the animator that we are finished, so the animator returns to
      its correct state and the graph allows more animation.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"9e9daaa6-f2c9-4fa3-9959-3b64befd74bc","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7505.0,"yMin":-547.0,"xMax":-7368.0,"yMax":-483.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"honestly,
      not sure. probably m/s?","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"1d6d829e-a05b-4cf9-aebe-ed4fa2db4972","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-9456.0,"yMin":849.0,"xMax":-9240.0,"yMax":942.0},"title":"Graveyard","body":"This
      long string is for if I ever want to try making dash defined as a distance
      instead of a force. For now, it is not worth it.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"a08374f4-c50c-4647-b3df-971090c0899b","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4311.0,"yMin":3988.0,"xMax":-4169.0,"yMax":4065.0},"title":"Attacking","body":"If
      the animator is turned off (if we are jumping) turn it on.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"c7ea0431-03ee-4ef2-b2f4-3f71c4df431d","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4488.0,"yMin":-824.0,"xMax":-4213.0,"yMax":-701.0},"title":"Jump
      Height","body":"To make the player jump a consistent height in m no matter
      what the gravity is.\nThe formula is yVelocity = sqrt(JumpHeight x gravity
      x -2), but there''s a delta time in there because Unity measures most things
      in m/s not timestep.","colorTheme":"Orange","guid":"2a859ead-85a4-4a70-a75d-40e78d630db7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8784.0,"yMin":-1334.0,"xMax":-8606.0,"yMax":-1252.0},"title":"Object","body":"This
      half controls the player object.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"67d0a846-4a01-4603-85f0-57b2b360c08e","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-4093.0,"yMin":-197.0,"xMax":-3956.0,"yMax":-116.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player can''t jump, check if they''re grounded.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"66af41e6-5c38-4c38-a27b-889ab05fbed7","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-5719.0,"yMin":-19.0,"xMax":-5492.667,"yMax":88.0},"title":"Movement","body":"If
      the player is giving an input, store the direction of that input. 1 is right
      and -1 is left, respective to the camera. If the player is not giving an input,
      set it to 0.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"48b5968f-e3d3-4bdb-b0b1-261afe5e9ba9","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8544.0,"yMin":-555.0,"xMax":-8407.0,"yMax":-491.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"metres/second","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"4f8205a5-f77f-4b0b-a668-10ae44434515","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-8399.0,"yMin":-332.0,"xMax":-8303.0,"yMax":-268.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"number","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"fdf2a9fa-ff55-45e2-a5d1-b510a85e1747","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-7945.0,"yMin":731.0,"xMax":-7797.0,"yMax":795.0},"title":"Initialise","body":"seconds,
      calculated rather than set","colorTheme":"Green","guid":"e4636de5-023c-4e66-a7c5-4ea644d5dcb4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"},{"position":{"xMin":-9604.0,"yMin":-31.0,"xMax":-9499.111,"yMax":33.0},"title":"Graveyard","body":"The
      projectile attack.","colorTheme":"Classic","guid":"1c7173d1-4ff2-4bca-ac2a-b78ec2f008f4","$type":"Unity.VisualScripting.StickyNote"}],"$version":"A"}}'
